                <pb facs="0195" n="91" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg91"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3690: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-01-29T10:00:00+08:00">January 29, 1932—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 29—4:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Japanese naval units now at Shanghai comprise: 17 destroyers, 4 cruisers, 1
                    aircraft carrier, 1 gunboat. Of these units 12 destroyers and 1 cruiser arrived
                    yesterday.</p>
                <p>Repeated to the Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
